## Finding

`SOURCE_PIXEL_939_ALPHA` remains open for `939.a`, `939.b`, `939.c`.
The affected author fields are `solutions.939.numeric_crossing`,
`solutions.939.tasks[0..2].answer`, and
`inventories.fig-64.queried_coordinates[0].x`.

The author leaves the numeric crossing and all three numeric answers null.
Its symbolic sets are `{alpha}`, `(alpha,5]`, and `[-2,alpha)`.
They agree structurally with the independent FIRST proof: a unique crossing,
the same inequality directions, exclusion of the crossing for strict
inequalities, and inclusion of the appropriate closed domain endpoints.
This is uncertainty about an unfilled source coordinate, not a wrong numeric
claim. The original author hold and null fields are not erased or filled.

The separate frozen FIRST inventory records `(1,-1/2)` at
`/exercises/1/source_inventory/queried_intersections/0`, giving `{1}`, `(1,5]`
and `[-2,1)`. That previously recorded observation is compatible with the
author's coarse bracket `0<alpha<2`. It is not a new pixel inspection, an
author infill, or approval of all 21 numeric author outputs.

